§ `s 205-30`

-- d072: Daniel, a director of the company that is the Foundation's trustee, is a responsible entity. d091: once he resigns he
-- is not (unless he goes on performing a director's duties, which the definition of director catches).
#ASSERT `Am I a responsible entity` `d072: Daniel, director of the Foundation's trustee company`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a responsible entity` `d091: Daniel after resigning as a director`

§ `s 205-15`

-- d072: a trust all of whose trustees are constitutional corporations is federally regulated -- as every private ancillary
-- fund must be (TAA s 426-105(1)(a)). A WA trust with individual trustees and no Territory link is not.
#ASSERT `Is my foundation a federally regulated entity` `d072: the Foundation, a trust with a company trustee`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation a federally regulated entity` `a WA charitable trust with individual trustees`

§ `s 205-35`

-- d072: a deductible gift recipient is not a basic religious charity, so the Foundation has no exemption from the governance
-- standards or reporting. A small unincorporated church with $20,000 in grants (not over $100,000) is one.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation a basic religious charity` `d072: the Foundation as a deductible gift recipient`
#ASSERT `Is my foundation a basic religious charity` `a small unincorporated church with 20000 in grants`

§ `s 45-10`

-- d072, d091: the Foundation is not a basic religious charity, so the governance standards bind it (their content is in the
-- undeposited Regulations). Advocacy that is not lawful is not protected from them.
#ASSERT `Can the governance standards bind my foundation` FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation's advocacy protected` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 205-25`

-- d072: with $2,000,000 revenue in 2050-51, the Foundation is large on the Act's figures ($250,000, $1,000,000). On thresholds
-- of $500,000 and $3,000,000 -- the encoder's UNVERIFIED understanding of what the 2022 Regulations prescribe, not read in any
-- deposit -- it would be medium. d091: on $120,000 in 2075-76 it is small. Exactly $250,000 is not "less than $250,000": medium.
-- (s 205-25(5): the Commissioner may keep last year's size -- an input.)
#ASSERT `What size is my foundation` 2000000 250000 1000000 FALSE `small` EQUALS `large`
#ASSERT `What size is my foundation` 2000000 500000 3000000 FALSE `small` EQUALS `medium`
#ASSERT `What size is my foundation` 120000 250000 1000000 FALSE `small` EQUALS `small`
#ASSERT `What size is my foundation` 250000 250000 1000000 FALSE `small` EQUALS `medium`

§ `ss 60-5, 60-10, 60-20, 60-25, 60-60`

-- d072: large in 2050-51, the Foundation lodges an information statement and an audited financial report. A medium
-- entity may have it reviewed instead (unless the Commissioner requires audit). d091: small in 2075-76, an information statement only.
#ASSERT `What must my foundation lodge` `large` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an information statement and an audited financial report`
#ASSERT `What must my foundation lodge` `medium` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an information statement and a financial report, reviewed or audited`
#ASSERT `What must my foundation lodge` `small` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an information statement only`

§ `ss 60-5(2), 60-10(2), 60-85(2)(b)`

-- d072: for the year ending 30 June 2051, by 31 December 2051. On a substituted accounting period ending 31 December
-- 2051, by 30 June 2052.
#ASSERT `By when must my foundation lodge` (Date 30 6 2051) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS (Date 31 12 2051)
#ASSERT `By when must my foundation lodge` (Date 31 12 2051) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS (Date 30 6 2052)

§ `s 60-65`

-- d091: small, an error found 1 September 2076 is corrected by 31 October 2076 (60 days; 28 if medium or large).
#ASSERT `By when must my foundation correct the error` `small` (Date 1 9 2076) EQUALS (Date 31 10 2076)

§ `s 55-5`

-- d072: the record of the $2,000,000 gift received 1 March 2051 is kept until 1 March 2058. The trustee company, a body
-- corporate, can be fined up to 5 x 20 penalty units: 5 x 20 x 330 = 33,000.
#ASSERT `Until when must my foundation keep the records` (Date 1 3 2051) EQUALS (Date 1 3 2058)

#ASSERT `What is the most my foundation can be fined for its records` TRUE 330 EQUALS 33000

§ `s 65-5`

-- d091: the change of directors -- of responsible entities -- must be notified. A breach that is not significant need not be
-- (under (1)(e)). Small, aware 3 May 2076: by 2 July 2076 (60 days). A significant
-- breach costing entitlement: 28 days, even for a small entity.
#ASSERT `Must my foundation notify the Commissioner` `d091: the children replace Daniel as directors`
#ASSERT NOT `Must my foundation notify the Commissioner` `a minor breach of a governance standard`

#ASSERT `By when must my foundation notify the Commissioner` `d091: the children replace Daniel as directors` `small` (Date 3 5 2076) EQUALS (Date 2 7 2076)
#ASSERT `By when must my foundation notify the Commissioner` `a significant breach costing it its entitlement` `small` (Date 3 5 2076) EQUALS (Date 31 5 2076)

§ `ss 80-5, 100-5`

-- d091: the Foundation is federally regulated, so a believed governance breach opens warnings and the suspension or removal
-- of a director the Commissioner considers necessary -- not if the Commissioner does not. A WA trust that is not federally
-- regulated can be warned only for an external conduct standard breach.
#ASSERT NOT `May my foundation be formally warned` `a WA trust, believed in breach of a governance standard`
#ASSERT `May my foundation be formally warned` `a WA trust, believed in breach of an external conduct standard`

#ASSERT `May I be suspended or removed` `d091: the Foundation, believed in breach of a governance standard` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May I be suspended or removed` `d091: the Foundation, believed in breach of a governance standard` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 100-20`

-- d091 variant: removed, Daniel ceases to be a director of the trustee company. Suspended until 1 December 2076
-- (HYPOTHETICAL), he is a director again on 2 December 2076 and may be a responsible entity again from 1 December 2076.
#ASSERT `Do I cease to be a director` `removed` TRUE (Date 1 9 2076) (Date 1 1 2000)
#ASSERT NOT `Do I cease to be a director` `suspended` TRUE (Date 2 12 2076) (Date 1 12 2076)

#ASSERT `May I become a responsible entity again` `suspended` (Date 1 12 2076) (Date 1 12 2076)

§ `s 100-25`

-- d091 variant: removed, Daniel commits an offence by instructing his children, knowing they act on his wishes; up to 1 year,
-- or 50 x 330 = 16,500, or both. An accountant's proper professional advice is not an offence.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by managing my foundation` `d091 variant: Daniel, removed, tells his children how to run the Foundation`
#ASSERT NOT `Do I commit an offence by managing my foundation` `a removed director's accountant advising the board in that capacity`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for managing while suspended` 330 EQUALS 16500

§ `ss 175-35, 175-40`

-- d072: large, the 2050-51 statement due 31 December 2051 lodged 31 January 2052 (31 days late: 2 periods, the Act's own
-- example) costs 2 x 5 x 330 = 3,300. d091: small, 200 days late (8 periods, capped at 5) costs 5 x 330 = 1,650. Medium, 28 days
-- late, 1 x 2 x 330 = 660.
#ASSERT `What penalty for lodging late` (Date 31 12 2051) (Date 31 1 2052) `large` 330 EQUALS 3300
#ASSERT `What penalty for lodging late` (Date 31 12 2076) (Date 19 7 2077) `small` 330 EQUALS 1650
#ASSERT `What penalty for lodging late` (Date 31 12 2051) (Date 28 1 2052) `medium` 330 EQUALS 660

§ `ss 175-10 to 175-30`

-- Recklessness: 40 x 330 = 13,200; with obstruction +20% = 15,840; disclosed before any examination, nil. Carelessness
-- disclosed during an examination, saving time, would be 6,600 - 1,320 = 5,280 (not asserted).
#ASSERT `Is my foundation liable for a false statement` `a reckless misstatement in the information statement`

#ASSERT `What penalty for a false statement` `a reckless misstatement in the information statement` 330 EQUALS 13200
#ASSERT `What penalty for a false statement` `a reckless misstatement, then obstruction` 330 EQUALS 15840
#ASSERT `What penalty for a false statement` `a reckless misstatement disclosed before any examination` 330 EQUALS 0

§ `ss 180-20, 180-25`

-- d091: the duty to notify the change of directors, arising 3 May 2076, is imposed on Anjali as a director then. d072:
-- Daniel is not personally liable for a penalty from an oversight, but is for one from his own deliberate false statement.
-- d091: Anjali is not liable for a penalty payable before she was a director. The Foundation's offences are not Daniel's:
-- s 180-25 reaches only trusts with no company trustee.
#ASSERT `Is my foundation's obligation also mine` TRUE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `Am I personally liable for my foundation's amount` `d072: Daniel, a late-lodgement penalty from an oversight`
#ASSERT `Am I personally liable for my foundation's amount` `d072 variant: Daniel, a penalty from his own deliberate false statement`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I personally liable for my foundation's amount` `d091: Anjali, for a penalty payable before she was a director`

#ASSERT NOT `Is my foundation's offence mine` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my foundation's offence mine` FALSE TRUE

